## 4. Source Stance

- Every factual statement, number, and quote must have a source link or clear source description.
- Every truth-like claim defaults to using an inline clickable short anchor.
- Every research artifact must end with a unified `## Resources` section.
- Source quality follows two tracks: disclosure-fact track `topic-local evidence cache > primary public > trusted third-party > web`; market-snapshot track `topic-local evidence cache / financial-data > trusted third-party > web`.
- Within the same quality tier, prioritize `home-market / local-language source`.
- `financial-data` is treated as the highest-value structured financial cache within the `topic-local evidence cache`; for market / snapshot fields, check it and local `_cache` first, then trusted third-party, and only then the web.
- `internet source` only fills gaps in the market-snapshot track; it must not impersonate company-disclosed fact. Company/disclosure facts still prioritize `primary public`.

The more complete claim-level source contract, fallback taxonomy, shared hook law, and skill-specific judgment / workflow delta are jointly determined by the invoked active skill and workspace hooks.

